From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: aswin-mcw <aswin.kalies@multicorewareinc.com>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 21:53:29 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 26/29] mingw: use mingw_pe_seh_emit_stackalloc in
 seh_pattern_emit

Upstream 5816e459964 ("Rename SEH functions for reuse in AArch64")
renamed seh_emit_stackalloc to mingw_pe_seh_emit_stackalloc.  Our own
rename commit was dropped during the rebase because upstream already
carries it, but our later commit "Fix unwiding codes when stack probing
is applied" adds call sites that still use the old name:

  winnt.cc:1527: error: 'seh_emit_stackalloc' was not declared in this scope
  winnt.cc:1537: error: 'seh_emit_stackalloc' was not declared in this scope

Upstream's rename is broader than ours was, so dropping ours left these
two call sites orphaned.  A sweep of the full rename map found no other
stale names.
---
 gcc/config/mingw/winnt.cc | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/gcc/config/mingw/winnt.cc b/gcc/config/mingw/winnt.cc
index 74ca1b44d94..5b728fa405b 100644
--- a/gcc/config/mingw/winnt.cc
+++ b/gcc/config/mingw/winnt.cc
@@ -1524,7 +1524,7 @@ seh_pattern_emit (FILE *f, struct seh_frame_state *seh, rtx pat)
 		increment = INTVAL (XEXP (src, 1));
 		src = XEXP (src, 0);
 		if (dest == stack_pointer_rtx)
-		  seh_emit_stackalloc (f, seh, increment);
+		  mingw_pe_seh_emit_stackalloc (f, seh, increment);
 		break;
 
 	      case MINUS:
@@ -1534,7 +1534,7 @@ seh_pattern_emit (FILE *f, struct seh_frame_state *seh, rtx pat)
 		extend = XEXP (extend, 1);
 		if (dest == stack_pointer_rtx && src == stack_pointer_rtx
 		    && REGNO(extend) == R12_REGNUM) 
-		  seh_emit_stackalloc (f, seh, stack_alloc);
+		  mingw_pe_seh_emit_stackalloc (f, seh, stack_alloc);
    	      break;
 
 	      case CONST_INT:
